# Nexus AI professional audit log

After you finish a **code fix**, **build verification**, or **push to `main`** in this repo, append a concise timestamped entry to **both** audit report paths — do this automatically without waiting to be asked.

## Destinations (write the same entry to both)

1. `C:\Users\faith\Documents\NEXUS_AI_PROFESSIONAL_AUDIT_REPORT.md`
2. `[Environment]::GetFolderPath('MyDocuments')\NEXUS_AI_PROFESSIONAL_AUDIT_REPORT.md`  
   (OneDrive Documents when redirected — currently `C:\Users\faith\OneDrive\Documents\...`)

If a path is missing, create the file (or copy from the other path) then append. Never skip logging because one path failed; still update the other.

## When to append

- Local `npm run build` / project build script succeeds or fails after a fix
- A commit lands on `main` (especially after `git push origin main` / `origin HEAD`)
- A Vercel/deploy-related build break is diagnosed and fixed

Skip chatter-only turns with no code, build, or push outcome.

## Entry format

Append under a running section (create `## Appendix — Agent activity log` before `*End of report.*` if needed):

```markdown
### YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM TZ — short title
- **Commit:** `hash` (or `uncommitted` / `n/a`)
- **Files:** comma-separated paths or `path (N files)`
- **Build / deploy:** pass/fail + command or “pushed → Vercel retrigger”
- **Summary:** one sentence on cause → fix → outcome
```

Keep each entry short. Prefer UTC or local wall time consistently. Do not dump full diffs or secrets.